Sedimentary Geology — John Southard, MIT 12.110 (@mp-mit-sedimentary: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_7FWZZ66CT5G1FP2JPQMWRV1YHM
John Southard. Sedimentary Geology, MIT 12.110, Spring 2007. [Official course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-110-sedimentary-geology-spring-2007/) · [Complete lecture-note sequence](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-110-sedimentary-geology-spring-2007/pages/lecture-notes/).

Read the full published notes, including sediment composition/textures, particle properties and transport, siliciclastic and carbonate rocks, chert/evaporites, diagenesis, environments, stratigraphy, basins, and organic resources. Focus the petrological studies on mineral/grain associations, provenance, reactions, textures, and burial alteration, returning to shared geology for wider landscape/history preparation.

The 2007 instructor/edition is distinct from David Mohrig's Fall 2004 OCW course. Preserve MIT OCW and component notices and identify any separate required readings. Identity, scope, resources, and source routes checked on 29 October 2026. Notes, images, and field material remain external references.

